    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/2946db5b310d3e24627457d7eecab16c115782862079366534a96472bd008c67.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The digitized ship sections are exported to Excel  in two columns (xz-plan) from Digitizer",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/9b14ebfa3f2036781bf8e2d4c7de6fba23ddc81f2565885a09fbf223a3d6bcef.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Example:",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "S175 container ship.",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Ascii file:",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "S175.mgf",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "09/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "6",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "ShipX (VERES) by MARINTEK",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/50ddad39a73c96c583997f0979d85c1d404dd497042456b35cf96934c89c5cbb.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "**MARINTEK** - the Norwegian Marine Technology Research Institute - does research and development in the maritime sector for industry and the public sector. The Institute develops and verifies technological solutions for the shipping and maritime equipment industries and for offshore petroleum production.",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<strong>VERES</strong> - <strong>VEssel RESponse program</strong> is a <strong><u>Strip Theory Program</u></strong> which calculates wave-induced loads on and motions of mono-hulls and barges in deep to very shallow water. The program is based on the famous paper by <strong>Salvesen</strong>, <strong>Tuck</strong> and <strong>Faltinsen</strong> (1970). <em>Ship Motions and Sea Loads</em>. Trans. SNAME.",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/e27d355a9393ecf736ff330929e4235af7928cd0e0bd405f8c4adc8cc9d4c436.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "09/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "7",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/294640336a47a67e1132c072ead384d4f72cef2fabec7fbb2a845675d2d74eb4.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "OCTOPUS SEAWAY by Amarcon",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "**and AMARCON cooperate in further development of SEAWAY**",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The Maritime Research Institute Netherlands (MARIN) and AMARCON agree to cooperate in further development of SEAWAY. MARIN is an internationally recognized authority on hydrodynamics, involved in frontier breaking research programs for the maritime and offshore industries and navies.",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/eaee2363f5ea9189e92962b27a828edc07fec50541f0cf596df296cb3937609c.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "SEAWAY is developed by Professor J.M.J. Journée at the Delft Univ. of Technology",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "SEAWAY is a <strong><u>Strip Theory Program</u></strong> to calculate wave-induced loads on and motions of mono-hulls and barges in deep to very shallow water. When not accounting for interaction effects between the hulls, also catamarans can be analyzed. Work of very acknowledged hydromechanic scientists (like Ursell, Tasai, Frank, Keil, Newman, Faltinsen, Ikeda, etc.) has been used, when developing this code.",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "SEAWAY has extensively been verified and validated using other computer",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "**codes and experimental data.**",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "09/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "9",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/36a7adbf2b23f90cce16168eee9ac26276585e8d47a488e1e951cab9408bc328.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "WAMIT (Vers. 6.3) by WAMIT INC.",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "**WAMIT®**  is the most advanced set of tools available for analyzing wave interactions with offshore platforms and other structures or vessels.",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "**WAMIT®**  was developed by **Professor Newman** and coworkers at **MIT** in 1987, and it has gained widespread recognition for its ability to analyze the complex structures with a high degree of accuracy and efficiency.",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/c5f09a38f6936d2222804ab8ae29808dfe059c4eb04e9993e799faa14bf1b065.png",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "3D Panelization of",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "a Supply Vessel",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Over the past 20 years WAMIT has been licensed to more than 90 industrial and research organizations worldwide.",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "09/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "11",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Hydrodynamic Methods (MSS Hydro)",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Frequency-Dependent Hydrodynamic Added Mass, Potential Damping, and Restoring Forces:   Computed using:  WAMIT, ShipX (VERES), or Octopus SEAWAY",
            "- Nonlinear Viscous Damping and Current Loads:",
            "    - ITTC quadratic drag formulation/ added resistance in surge (includes current)",
            "    - Nonlinear cross-flow drag in sway and yaw (includes currents)",
            "    - Munk moment in yaw from potential coefficients",
            "    - Higher order nonlinear damping terms in heave, roll, and pitch (manually added)",
            "    - Maneuvering coefficients (manually added)"
        ],
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Nonlinear Frequency-Dependent Damping in Roll due to Bilge Keels and Anti-Rolling Tanks: Can be computed in ShipX (VERES) and Octopus (SEAWAY)",
            "- Frequency-Dependent Linear Viscous Damping in DOFs 1,2,6:  Manually added using exponential decaying functions for skin friction",
            "- Wave Loads:  1st-order (Froude-Krylov and diffraction) and 2nd-order wave loads (wave drift) are computed using 2D/3D potential theory",
            "- Wind Loads:  Computed using wind coefficient tables"
        ],
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "09/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "12",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Output (Ascii-files) from Hydrodynamic Codes",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- VERES",
            "    - \\*.re1",
            "    - \\*.re2"
        ],
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- SeaWay",
            "    - \\*.out",
            "- WAMIT",
            "    - \\*.x"
        ],
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "09/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "13",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Postprocessing of the Hydrodynamic Data Files to the MSS vessel structure",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Extract necessary information from the ASCII files generated by the hydrodynamic code",
            "- Scaling of data",
            "- Change and translate coordinate frames for hydrodynamic coefficients, RAOs, transfer functions etc.",
            "- Add viscous effects (hydrodynamic codes are non-viscous/potential theory)",
            "- Process data for time-domain simulation"
        ],
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Notice that the *MSS vessel structure* is independent of the hydrodynamic code!",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "**MSS Hydro toolbox commands:** >> veres2vessel.m",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": ">> wamit2vessel.m",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": ">> seaway2vessel.m",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "09/09/2007",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "14",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "MSS Hydro Vessel Structure",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 14
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- xxx"
        ],
        "page_idx": 14
    },
    {
